tsdemux: a packet that starts a PES after a continuity break is kept

GStreamer 1.26.11 tsdemux drops the pending PES on a continuity_counter
mismatch -- right, it may be short -- and then the mismatching packet
itself, even when it starts a new PES. ISO/IEC 13818-1 2.4.3.3: what was
lost is before it. Replayed (mediabox-live engine_tests
a_multiplex_hole_*): after a 480 ms hole on every PID the first video
unit past it was lost; a key frame there costs a GOP.

--- a/gst/mpegtsdemux/tsdemux.c
+++ b/gst/mpegtsdemux/tsdemux.c
@@ -3898,7 +3898,12 @@
         }
         stream->state = PENDING_PACKET_EMPTY;
 
-        return GST_FLOW_OK;
+        /* A packet that starts a PES (payload_unit_start_indicator) begins
+         * a new, whole unit: what was lost is before it (ISO/IEC 13818-1
+         * 2.4.3.3). Dropping it too lost the first unit after every break,
+         * a key frame and a GOP's wait when the break ended at one. */
+        if (!packet->payload_unit_start_indicator)
+          return GST_FLOW_OK;
       }
     }
   }
